  "conclusions": {
    "low_iou": "V2 optimizes sequential value-state risk, not top attention mass. Projected/full-dimensional V mask IoU is 0.858 on six snapshots, while either V mask/control IoU is 0.156; the low control overlap is therefore objective and reuse related, not mainly rank32 projection error.",
    "online_gap": "Online selection lacks future row-normalized denominator and complete future value direction at the decision point. It can be self-consistent with an alternative support, but it changes the sampler trajectory; the full-dimensional diagnostic at threshold0.027 kept fewer tiles and had higher operator error, so full V alone does not remove the gap.",
    "trajectory": "On the completed 503-item audit, V2 had mean denoising delta -29.07 vs control; among V2-only correct items delta was -198.87, while control-only items had +204.25. Shorter trajectories are a real basin change, not simply early truncation.",
    "refinement": "The complete jcgate audit is negative for the stated objective: 256/503 (50.9%) versus control 268/503 (53.3%), -2.39 percentage points (paired exact p=0.207; bootstrap 95% CI shown above). Row protection reduced GLOBAL sparsity to 78.07% from 83.16% while lowering accuracy, so it is rejected before timing. The remaining candidate should be a fixed-budget mass-gated value selector, not another uncalibrated row-weight threshold."
  },
